    "Cleanup options:\n",
    "- resample boundary then resolve collisions using the feature transformation\n",
    "- prune segments using the region adjacency graph -- if the shared boundary is larger than some fraction of the total perimeter, then merge if the colors are similar enough and the statistics of the merged shapes are not too far degraded\n",
    "- After the first pass finding the most probable floe, compute an average using the stack of all the candidate shapes with Gaussian blur, then fit a contour to the result.\n",
    "- Subtract the final result, check for small floes in the residual\n",
    "- Loop through the final floes, use structuring element with appropriate size scale\n",
    "- Remove / flag floes bounded by clouds."
