   "source": [
    "## Simple binary image cleanup method\n",
    "- Erode first to limit the chances of the fill holes flooding everything\n",
    "- Keep the filled regions where the icemask or the cloud mask are positive\n",
    "- Use the filled mask to fill interior holes in the kmeans result. Won't catch holes near floe edges."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "5bc06049-9a08-42b5-988e-417014b04ca3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "    clean_binary_floes(binary_img, icemask, cloudmask; strel=strel_box((7,7)), max_fill=50)\n",
    "\n",
    "Fill holes in a binarized sea ice image by masking internal holes where \n",
    "the preliminary ice mask or the cloud mask are positive. This means that\n",
    "cloud speckle should be filled, but that large clouds shouldn't be.\n",
    "\"\"\"\n",
    "function clean_binary_floes(binary_img, icemask, cloudmask; erosion_strel=strel_box((7,7)), filling_strel=strel_diamond((5,5)), max_fill=100)\n",
    "    out = deepcopy(binary_img)\n",
    "    # 1. Shrink objects using the provided structuring element\n",
    "    eroded_img = erode(out, strel)\n",
    "\n",
    "    # 2. After shrinking, \n",
    "    filled = fill_holes(eroded_img, filling_strel) # Test how permissive this is. Should we use imfill instead?\n",
    "    filled .= filled .&& (icemask .|| cloudmask)\n",
    "    filled .= .!imfill(.!filled, (0, max_fill))\n",
    "    closing!(filled)\n",
    "    out[filled .> 0] .= 1\n",
    "    return out\n",
    "end"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "7e1fddb4-c3d6-4f5a-a528-b79274b84f8b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "?fill_holes"
   ]
  },
